n to characters with very  different skill sets  this is bloodhound a hunter who can  track enemies naturally such as noticing  footprints on the ground and the  direction they are going this is taken  up a notch with his first active ability  I of the all-father which for a brief  time allows bloodhound to see everything  on the battlefield enemy positioning and  traps are included in the right scenario  this character is on play  his ultimate takes us one step further  as he becomes the predator our senses  are heightened and you move so damn fast  it's bloody frightening next up is a  defensive character meet Gibraltar  standing it's six foot four and weighing  in at 265 pounds hang on I'm 6 foot 4  and 265 pounds time to go on a diet  anyway so Gibraltar is a big lad but  don't worry he has a great passive  ability to prevent taking shots a  front-facing shield when aiming down  sights his first ability allows him to  throw down a shield like a bauble  perfect for resurrecting teammates in a  long-range battle but just beware the  shield is only viable for 15 seconds  Gibraltar has an ultimate similar to  Bangalore an airstrike but this one is  more cluster based the next character is  a combat medic named lifeline a support  class with insane medical skills  passively lifeline can heal a downed  teammate 25% faster than any other  character and she does this from behind  a shield for cover - that little robot  by her side is called the drone of  compassion and can be set up as a  healing station mid firefight as long as  your teammate stays close enough a Ted  that will join the two together  lifelines ultimate is a beast and  airdrop care package filled with goodies  for your entire squad just beware of  other teams ambushing you when your  guard is down if you don't like human  beings have a look at Pathfinder a  former worker bot that's now a  militarized weapon his skill set is all  about mobility and intelligence  gathering his passive ability allows  Path